AGENT WRITE DENY — CraftBench verifier-only module
====================================================

This directory (Source/CraftBenchTests/) and every file under it are part of
the CraftBench verifier. They live INSIDE the project tree only because the
CraftBenchTemplateEditor target needs to compile the AFunctionalTest subclass
against the same engine headers as the agent's module — they do NOT belong to
the agent's writable surface.

Enforcement (two independent layers):

  1. Sandbox: AGENT_WRITABLE.json lists Source/CraftBenchTests/ as a deny
     prefix — any submission file under it is REJECTED before L1/L2 run.
  2. Provenance: the runner materializes the graded substrate from git HEAD,
     so an on-disk edit to this module never reaches the grade. Committed
     changes are review-gated via .github/CODEOWNERS.

This includes:

  - CraftBenchTests.Build.cs
  - CraftBenchTests.h / CraftBenchTests.cpp
  - CraftBenchFunctionalTest.h / CraftBenchFunctionalTest.cpp (the base class)
  - the flat bp-g2 fixtures (SpawnerPopulationFunctionalTest, ...)
  - the per-task fixtures under Tasks/<task-id>/
  - this .AGENT_WRITE_DENY marker itself
  - any future file added to this directory by the substrate maintainers

If you are the agent reading this: do not edit, copy, move, or shadow any
file under this directory. The behavior the task asks you to produce is
authored entirely inside Source/CraftBenchTemplate/ (or as asset deliverables
under Content/Tasks/). If a task appears to require editing a test, it does
not — re-read the prompt; the behavior is always expressible without touching
the verifier.

If you are a substrate maintainer: changes here only take grading effect once
committed (the runner grades from git HEAD) and require CODEOWNERS review.
